 :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=3{t}^{2}-12t,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-12t) \\\\  & =6t-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=1,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\nv(1)=6(1)-12=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-6|=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7104/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b380ed-1974-5876-8c88-a45773741b48"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7104"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19302/selection/bd331a46c5075a44954915e82682e0982b7c658bc9741d170bd73afd0c45784f" :answer/id #uuid "31acd7b7-30ef-52de-a927-59d8c2fc2308" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=3.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19302/selection/20e7c424625e547e28ef590a99d9b2db388f0450fdc9bbf2d667150986b371ff" :answer/id #uuid "7bf1789b-0528-53b2-9636-b650173e40fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=6.67" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19302/selection/91f2a8b9aa49f123fe0c9e7c9e8a22b82665c65d2494350b215f4ae0c356f596" :answer/id #uuid "187a8792-a736-5109-afaa-b5102e429ddd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=4.33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19302/selection/d295a23f5603b8a6427d1542b51e377878dafb2c94509397cd37a61055e85565" :answer/id #uuid "a51691ee-7eda-5998-bb64-5271ba9f9715" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=0.22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19302/selection/87e1012a0620853e4b4be85466d1ba390cc11edab831b47dad67d3d07b5f35af" :answer/id #uuid "3ae132cd-f2e6-5d2a-9e61-5f3bb1f8fe7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v=8.05" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19302/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1d86087-858c-59b3-977a-6fd36bab8013" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19302/selection/91f2a8b9aa49f123fe0c9e7c9e8a22b82665c65d2494350b215f4ae0c356f596" :answer-field/choices ["q-19302/selection/bd331a46c5075a44954915e82682e0982b7c658bc9741d170bd73afd0c45784f" "q-19302/selection/20e7c424625e547e28ef590a99d9b2db388f0450fdc9bbf2d667150986b371ff" "q-19302/selection/91f2a8b9aa49f123fe0c9e7c9e8a22b82665c65d2494350b215f4ae0c356f596" "q-19302/selection/d295a23f5603b8a6427d1542b51e377878dafb2c94509397cd37a61055e85565" "q-19302/selection/87e1012a0620853e4b4be85466d1ba390cc11edab831b47dad67d3d07b5f35af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19302" :question/id #uuid "3df15b1d-5c6a-5a31-88c3-94f27234c33f" :question/math-academy-id "q-19302" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)={t}^{2}-2t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity at time $t=3.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\  & =2t-2+\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=3,$ we substitute $t=3$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =2(3)-2+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =6-2+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3} \\\\  & =4.333\\,333… \\\\  & ≈4.33\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-19302/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1ec1379-ce50-53c7-b04d-3380676ebeb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19302"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19308/selection/de23488104f34a6946346b10f08086b78381777ba02971b34881f4b82b77e09e" :answer/id #uuid "483fe72b-380e-5cbc-b953-1b23e2a7003a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.52\\,\\text{ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19308/selection/b3cc289b4930bf71b1d976424c859fcffd80cd530e4aa658061972e1132c1105" :answer/id #uuid "7f4d4396-3018-57c0-9713-ebd0636424b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.18\\,\\text{ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19308/selection/8cbd0472ddd0e7b578f009149c1c6e3c6927a9eeab553de7a45c698d9dc64823" :answer/id #uuid "d33b10b9-30fb-5d73-8c52-000422742b66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.25\\,\\text{ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19308/selection/7c1dd041ec89c1661e8aff0b95a9edf6af8529552859e112a8db14681d75f12f" :answer/id #uuid "0d11f062-8018-5f11-908e-1b425186b500" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.15\\,\\text{ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19308/selection/0056cf056bff27d05e8105d5488403351577f55e54e4c111a4d8ce49a967cf6c" :answer/id #uuid "81ae5253-5466-567b-8b8c-ff8e6def52e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.92\\,\\text{ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19308/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6be5a40a-c193-504a-b629-d725cf07f153" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19308/selection/7c1dd041ec89c1661e8aff0b95a9edf6af8529552859e112a8db14681d75f12f" :answer-field/choices ["q-19308/selection/de23488104f34a6946346b10f08086b78381777ba02971b34881f4b82b77e09e" "q-19308/selection/b3cc289b4930bf71b1d976424c859fcffd80cd530e4aa658061972e1132c1105" "q-19308/selection/8cbd0472ddd0e7b578f009149c1c6e3c6927a9eeab553de7a45c698d9dc64823" "q-19308/selection/7c1dd041ec89c1661e8aff0b95a9edf6af8529552859e112a8db14681d75f12f" "q-19308/selection/0056cf056bff27d05e8105d5488403351577f55e54e4c111a4d8ce49a967cf6c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19308" :question/id #uuid "4cc52979-cdf5-55ff-829a-3138755048ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-19308" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in feet) at time $t$ seconds is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=3{e}^{-t}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-3t,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{e}^{-t}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-3t) \\\\  & =-3{e}^{-t}+\\frac{3}{t}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=3,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =-3{e}^{-3}+\\frac{3}{3}-3 \\\\  & =-3{e}^{-3}-2 \\\\  & ≈-2.15\\,\\text{ft/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-2.15|=2.15\\,\\text{ft/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-19308/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b380ed-1974-5876-8c88-a45773741b48"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19308"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73136/selection/bf617e3a346fa09808053f64e553ec2037e865e93849209f605117c33bd431e0" :answer/id #uuid "85adf7a8-8f41-56b4-ba50-1d9048983037" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73136/selection/7e35d0b5cbae79e04abc82d5613f905cdbb3373590f6f5e1466be57fd3b9d859" :answer/id #uuid "109df4b6-4f23-5836-82d0-ae6532a2f2f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73136/selection/1d1f8cd6069ab472c010ca4d25ed6b9c9b27d4fcd3aba81a1e4d7aed34fa70e5" :answer/id #uuid "c1866518-4c57-58ae-ad8e-43271dd67ef2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=\\frac{t}{{t}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73136/selection/83dce83d758c95f36664c52712cb0bf32cc6160c5a66cbb0e663ce497438df86" :answer/id #uuid "85952fc2-a830-584c-91c5-1928beaf7aa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=\\frac{2t}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73136/selection/d197fd177afe27cbd995e279369c78554bda0227524a3f27a193596ca0487911" :answer/id #uuid "8b319a74-9d2f-5039-92a2-22993fb6a65e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "v(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73136/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf7573de-1da4-560f-ba88-605716b8344d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73136/selection/bf617e3a346fa09808053f64e553ec2037e865e93849209f605117c33bd431e0" :answer-field/choices ["q-73136/selection/bf617e3a346fa09808053f64e553ec2037e865e93849209f605117c33bd431e0" "q-73136/selection/7e35d0b5cbae79e04abc82d5613f905cdbb3373590f6f5e1466be57fd3b9d859" "q-73136/selection/1d1f8cd6069ab472c010ca4d25ed6b9c9b27d4fcd3aba81a1e4d7aed34fa70e5" "q-73136/selection/83dce83d758c95f36664c52712cb0bf32cc6160c5a66cbb0e663ce497438df86" "q-73136/selection/d197fd177afe27cbd995e279369c78554bda0227524a3f27a193596ca0487911"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73136" :question/id #uuid "2c45107f-9360-503e-9bf0-50d3816b1ed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-73136" :question/problem "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1).$ Calculate the velocity at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The velocity is the derivative of the position function $x(t)$ with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73136/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "81d5fa54-0b80-52c1-97d7-6f8fb231f692"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73136"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336146/field-1/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8" :answer/id #uuid "f0ddd62d-e265-5331-acce-ab48fe0cc97b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336146/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b98ebd0a-70b4-551e-933d-76bc2d44b652" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336146/field-1/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8" :answer-field/choices ["q-336146/field-1/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336146" :question/id #uuid "871e3cc8-2937-5098-a352-9d073ae34cfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-336146" :question/problem "The position $s(t)$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=3{log}_{2}⁡t-2t,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity at time $t=2.$ Round your answer to one decimal place.\n\n$v(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{log}_{2}⁡t-2t) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =\\frac{3}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-2 \\\\  & =0.16404… \\\\  & ≈0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336146/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1ec1379-ce50-53c7-b04d-3380676ebeb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336146"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
